35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows our allocation is down a quarter, and off-site contacts earn nothing. We must build programs that generate on-site revenue to survive.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth, but the joint clinic collapsed. We need programs with proven, self-sustaining outcomes, not fragile partnerships.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Nine unfilled nursing posts and rising agency costs are alarming. Yet midwifery has unexpected slack. We must place new work where the team is actually stable, not where it’s already breaking.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, the car park fills before eleven! That’s a huge bottleneck. If we add more patients, the whole system will seize up. We need to check if the booking system can handle the overflow.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,My findings confirm my fears. The joint clinic collapsed because neither department owned the rota. We must avoid partnerships where responsibility is shared but never truly held.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, your caution is wise. The joint clinic’s failure mirrors my financial concern. We must avoid shared structures that dilute accountability and revenue.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, precisely. The data proves single-department ownership works. Shared structures are administrative noise. We must fund what actually sustains itself, not what looks good on paper.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree. But stability is just as vital as ownership. We cannot place new work on a team already drowning in agency cover.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, exactly! If the car park is full, adding more patients just creates chaos. We need a program that fits into the existing flow, not one that breaks it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, you are right. Stability is the foundation. I will ensure we choose a program where one team truly owns the work, so it does not unravel later.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, your staffing insight is critical. We must pair a stable team with a model that generates on-site revenue. Let us find that intersection.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, revenue is secondary to efficacy. The call-back trial proved single-department ownership works. We must fund a program that sustains itself without external partners or fragile shared rotas.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, I hear you. But revenue means nothing if the team collapses. We must prioritize the midwifery slack to ensure the program actually runs smoothly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, I agree! But if the booking system can’t track it, it’s invisible. We need a program that fits the current slots and doesn’t clog the car park!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree. The data agreements took fourteen months. We cannot build on such fragile ground. Let us choose a program that stands firmly on its own.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, I concur. We need a program that stands alone, generating on-site revenue without the fragility of shared partnerships. Let us seek that stability.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, I agree. The evidence is clear. We must select a program with single-department ownership and proven efficacy. Let us stop funding administrative noise.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree on single-department ownership. But we must also respect the staffing reality. Let us choose a program that fits the midwifery slack, not the broken nursing rosters.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I agree! Midwifery slack is great, but we still need space. Let’s pick a program that fits the existing slots and doesn’t clog the car park!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I agree. A program that fits our current space and staffing is wise. Let us choose something that will still be standing in year two, not just year one.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
